From df9ecc1f74d75a2c0f913c5ce81a57b1f7353030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:58:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] W1 collision arms (N1): upstream IQ4_XS mat-vec shader, MMVQ
 body and route as runtime switches beside ours, default ours

W1 dropped upstream df750f76b (IQ4_XS f32 mat-vec, 8 threads per superblock) and the b1ff4ca23 MMVQ body/route in favour of ours (lane-209 7062c6794 shader, R75 K=16 body, default legacy). Runbook 4.1b item 3 needs three arms on one binary. GGML_ARIFI_IQ4XS_MV=upstream loads df750f76b's shader (verbatim, mul_mat_vec_iq4_xs_up.comp). GGML_ARIFI_IQ4XS_MMVQ_BODY=upstream loads b1ff4ca23's K_PER_ITER 32 body with its std-quant rows. GGML_ARIFI_IQ4XS_MMVQ=upstream hands IQ4_XS to upstream's generic MMVQ rule. Exact strings only; unset = ours, byte-for-byte the W1 default path.

lane-296 ladder (test-backend-ops perf, served IQ4_XS shapes, n=1..9, 4 counterbalanced rounds): ours (f32, legacy route) is kept. Upstream's route loses at n=5..8 (MMVQ upstream body geomean 0.50-0.68x of ours; upstream f32 shader 0.35-0.77x). n=1..4 upstream body +0.5..1.6% geomean, not adopted: q8_1 path, R75's q8_1 admit failed greedy identity 3/12; owed a greedy gate. Correctness: MUL_MAT iq4_xs 96/96 on every arm, MUL_MAT_ID 5/5.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-296 W1 collision maker, Opus 5.5); upstream kernels from df750f76b and b1ff4ca23 (ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT)
Measured-effect: none on the default path (switches unset); arms receipts C:/ArifiLabs/cache/lane296/ev/B*-*.txt, ladder.txt
Lane: lane-296
